# The live suite (decision 0043 §1). On a machine with no
# GDRIVE_CLI_E2E_FOLDER it skips and the push goes through (§3); on a
# configured one a failure stops the branch before it leaves the machine.
if ! bun run test:e2e; then
  # 0012's CRITICAL policy, printed at the one moment anybody reads it. A fake
  # can only confirm what its author believed the API does; Google is the only
  # party that can contradict them, and this is it doing so (0043 Context).
  cat <<'POLICY'

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
E2E failed. Do NOT add mocks to bypass it, do NOT change expected values to
match broken behaviour, and do NOT skip or delete the test. Investigate the
root cause and fix the implementation.
  — decisions/0012-testing-strategy.md, "E2E policy (CRITICAL)"

The failing file's folder is left in Drive on purpose: the contents are the
evidence (decisions/0043-e2e-runs-before-push.md §2).
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

POLICY
  exit 1
fi
